{"Title":"An Act relative to waiving education requirements for skilled veterans to be LPNs","BillNumber":"S2327","DocketNumber":"SD934","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T13:36:01.373"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T13:36:01.3733333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2327/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Lewis, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2327) of Jason M. Lewis for legislation relative to waiving education requirements for skilled veterans to be LPNs.  Veterans and Federal Affairs.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 112 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting, after section 76B the following section:-\r\n\tSection 76C. The board of registration in nursing shall create a waiver program for military personnel who satisfactorily complete medical training offered through the military so that they may sit for the licensed practical nursing certification without the need to graduate from an approved practical nursing program.\r\n\tSECTION 2. The department of public health shall promulgate regulations no later than January 1, 2024.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J31"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}